{% macro content(spec) %}
{# Case-study system (ticket 20): the markdown-pipeline components and the
   width system (DR-0009), rendered with the REAL classes so this guide
   cannot drift from the code. The `case-study document-text` wrapper
   activates the scoped component styles. #}
{% set spec = spec or {} %}
{% set _class = spec.class or '' %}
{% set _content = spec.content or '{}' %}

<article class="gallery-text">
  <h2 class="page-header">Case-study system</h2>
  <div class="text-block">
    <p>The case-study pages render from markdown (see AUTHORING.md). Their
    layout has one text edge, bullet plates and cards inside the
    container, display boxes that bleed one indent step into the margins,
    and a full-bleed tier for media and background sections.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Type roles -->
  <div class="text-block">
    <h3 class="page-header">Type roles</h3>
    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <p style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px;">Headline — h2, 28.8px / 700</p>
      <p style="font-size: 1.17rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 8px;">Sub-head — h3, 22.5px / 700</p>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 4px;">Body copy — 18.4px / 300. One size for paragraphs and list text.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: #66686d; margin: 0;">Label — 15.4px (eyebrows, notes, captions). Never below this size.</p>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top: 8px;">Indent token: <code>$cs-indent = 28px</code> — box padding, box
    bleed, timeline gutter and marker hang all derive from it.</p>
    <p style="margin-top: 8px;">Content width: <strong>900/836</strong> — one content width
    site-wide (DR-0013); every page's text column is the container's 836px
    inner width at 1440.</p>
    <p style="margin-top: 8px;">List-context rule (DR-0010): <code>- item</code> at section
    level → fact chip; <code>- item</code> inside a box → plain bullet;
    <code>* item</code> → plain bullet list at section level (the opt-out);
    <code>1. step</code> → numbered timeline everywhere.</p>
    <p style="margin-top: 8px;">Chip plate: one token, <code>--cs-chip-plate</code>
    (white 0.45; the dark ground's documented instance is 0.06 — DR-0012).
    Bullet geometry: the dot sits 20px inside the plate, text 8px clear of
    the dot; plateless lists keep the dot ON the text edge (tickets 39/41).</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Width tiers -->
  <div class="text-block">
    <h3 class="page-header">Width tiers</h3>
    <p><strong>Text edge</strong> — all body copy aligns here.
    <strong>Bleed</strong> — display boxes (summary, quote groups, cols)
    extend one indent step into each margin. <strong>Full-bleed</strong> —
    media, tables and <code>full</code>-flagged containers span the
    viewport. Bullet plates (chips, plain lists) and cards sit WITHIN the
    container (tickets 39/53).</p>
    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <div class="cs-summary"><em>Bleed example — the summary box extends
        past the text edge by one indent step on both sides.</em></div>
    </div>
    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <div class="cs-cards">
        <div class="cs-card">
          <h3>Within the container — card (ticket 53)</h3>
          <p>The card's box spans the text column; its text sits inset
          inside the plate, like the chips.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <div class="cs-full" style="background-color: rgba(24, 24, 27, 0.12); border-radius: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: center; margin: 0;">Full-bleed band — <code>::: type full</code>
        (the background spans the viewport; content keeps its insets)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Vertical rhythm -->
  <div class="text-block">
    <h3 class="page-header">Vertical rhythm</h3>
    <p>One spacing scale governs all vertical gaps: <strong>8 / 16 / 24 /
    32 / 48 / 64 / 96</strong> (8pt grid). Roles: 8 inside components,
    16 list rhythm, 24 around media and after headings, 32 around
    self-contained blocks, 48 around media wrappers and h2→h3, 64 around
    pull quotes, 96 section padding. Label+content pairs (eyebrow →
    heading, sub-title → list) sit tight by design.</p>
    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <div style="background: rgba(24,24,27,0.08); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 8px;">8</div>
      <div style="background: rgba(24,24,27,0.08); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 16px;">16</div>
      <div style="background: rgba(24,24,27,0.08); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 24px;">24</div>
      <div style="background: rgba(24,24,27,0.08); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px;">32</div>
      <div style="background: rgba(24,24,27,0.08); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 48px;">48</div>
      <div style="background: rgba(24,24,27,0.08); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 64px;">64</div>
      <div style="background: rgba(24,24,27,0.08); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px; text-align: center;">96</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Heroes (ticket 45, DR-0014) -->
  <div class="text-block">
    <h3 class="page-header">Heroes</h3>
    <p>One hero component, one spacing/type set (DR-0014): eyebrow → h1
    16, h1 → summary 24, summary → details 24, padding 64/64. The variant
    picks <strong>ground and ink only</strong> — <strong>cover</strong>
    (full-bleed colored band, white ink), <strong>meta</strong> (in-flow,
    KPIs under the cover), <strong>adapted bare</strong> (transparent —
    the page's ground carries it, e.g. visuAI's dark page, with an
    adapted kicker instead of "Case Study"), and the mid-page
    <code>::: hero</code> from markdown.</p>

    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      {# guide-ladder note: demo titles are h2 (one h1 per page); the
         guide-flat-title class neutralizes the h2-in-hero's 16px padding
         so the demo shows the DR-0014 gaps exactly #}
      <header class="cs-hero guide-flat-title">
        <p class="cs-eyebrow">The visuAI Workflow</p>
        <h2>Adapted bare hero</h2>
        <p class="cs-cover-summary">Transparent on any ground — no cover box,
        an adapted eyebrow instead of the case-study kicker.</p>
        <p class="cs-cover-details">Design Lead ⋅ 2026</p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <section class="cs-hero cs-hero--meta">
        <div class="cs-metrics">
          <div class="cs-metric">
            <span class="cs-metric-value">15</span><span class="cs-metric-suffix">%</span>
            <span class="cs-metric-label">meta hero — KPIs sit under the cover</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <header class="cs-hero cs-hero--red guide-flat-title">
        <p class="cs-eyebrow">Case Study</p>
        <h2>Cover hero</h2>
        <p class="cs-cover-summary">White-on-color ink; the real cover spans
        the viewport (100vw technique, 64px/48px padding — DR-0014). This
        demo shows its structure at container width.</p>
        <p class="cs-cover-details">Details line</p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      {# the real ::: hero output — its h2 keeps the h1 look via the
         component's secondary-hero rule (16px vertical padding included) #}
      <header class="cs-hero">
        <p class="cs-eyebrow">Section Label</p>
        <h2>Mid-page hero</h2>
        <p class="cs-subtitle">Emitted by the ::: hero container in markdown —
        64/64 padding, subtitle and byline on the shared 24 gaps (DR-0014).</p>
      </header>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Components -->
  <div class="text-block">
    <h3 class="page-header">Components</h3>
    <div class="case-study document-text" style="padding-top: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px;">
      <ul class="cs-facts">
        <li>Fact chip — key stats and proof points</li>
        <li>Second chip — dot 20px inside the plate, text 8px clear of the dot (tickets 39/41)</li>
      </ul>

      <p style="margin-top: 16px;"><code>* item</code> at section level — the plain bullet list
      (<code>ul.cs-plain</code>, DR-0010): chip geometry, no plate.</p>
      <ul class="cs-plain">
        <li>Plain bullet — the dot sits ON the text edge, text +8px</li>
        <li>Second plain bullet — the opt-out when a list should not be a chip</li>
      </ul>

      <ol class="cs-timeline" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <li><h3>Timeline step one</h3><p>Real markup: ol.cs-timeline > li — the numbered dot and connector are the component's.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Timeline step two</h3><p>Numbers baseline-align with their titles.</p></li>
      </ol>

      <p class="cs-note">Note — [note: text], the muted annotation line with its icon.</p>

      <blockquote class="cs-quote" style="margin: 32px auto;">
        <p>"Display quote — centered, italic, h2-size, on every page."</p>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="cs-quotes">
        <div class="cs-quote"><blockquote><p>"Quote group — runs of 2+ quotes share one bleeding plate."</p></blockquote></div>
        <div class="cs-quote"><blockquote><p>"Each quote keeps its own blockquote inside the group."</p></blockquote></div>
      </div>

      <p class="cs-summary"><em>Summary box — [summary: text]; the bleeding closing-summary of a case study.</em></p>

      <p style="margin-top: 16px;">Image run (ticket 61): <code>::: shots</code> — N images
      side by side, each image's alt text = its caption below. Wraps on
      narrow screens.</p>
      <div class="cs-wide cs-wide--full">
        <div class="cs-shots">
          {# ticket 16 made these eager (the panel ships [hidden], so lazy
             images in a display:none subtree never hydrated and the row
             rendered collapsed until scrolled). Ticket 38 refines it:
             when this block renders inside the /workflow/ design panel
             (spec.lazyDemo), the thumbs ship loading="lazy" - they stop
             weighing on every visit - and tabs.js flips them eager on the
             panel's FIRST activation, so the row is still complete the
             moment the tab opens. The standalone /styleguide/ page calls
             this without lazyDemo and keeps eager loading. #}
          <figure class="cs-shot">
            <img src="../images/work/thumbs/gallery_thumb_artent.jpg" alt="Art-Ent — connecting artists and students"{% if spec.lazyDemo %} loading="lazy"{% endif %}>
            <figcaption>Art-Ent — the first shot's caption</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="cs-shot">
            <img src="../images/work/thumbs/gallery_thumb_climateclock.jpg" alt="Climate Clock — the second shot"{% if spec.lazyDemo %} loading="lazy"{% endif %}>
            <figcaption>Climate Clock — the second shot's caption</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="cs-shot">
            <img src="../images/work/thumbs/gallery_thumb_closet.jpg" alt="Digital Closet — the third shot"{% if spec.lazyDemo %} loading="lazy"{% endif %}>
            <figcaption>Digital Closet — the third shot's caption</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-divider" role="separator"><span>Divider</span></div>

      <div class="cs-frame" style="min-height: 120px;">
        <span class="cs-frame-label"><strong>Frame</strong>placeholder for mockups and pending media</span>
      </div>

      <p class="cs-frame-caption">Frame caption — a [point:] under an image renders
      as a dotless, italic caption (DR-0011)</p>

      <div class="cs-metrics" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <div class="cs-metric">
          <span class="cs-metric-value">15</span><span class="cs-metric-suffix">%</span>
          <span class="cs-metric-label">metric chip</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Color tokens (ticket 20) -->
  <div class="text-block">
    <h3 class="page-header">Color tokens</h3>
    <p>The case-study system's seven verified tokens (ticket 20), used as
    grounds, accents and inks across the themes. Contrast rationale lives
    at each usage site in <code>_case-study.scss</code>.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <span class="box-container" style="background: #111111;color: #ebf5ff;padding:8px;font-weight:700;">
          #111111
          <p>cs-black — fashion ground/accent</p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <span class="box-container" style="background: #0e7d6f;color: #ebf5ff;padding:8px;font-weight:700;">
          #0E7D6F
          <p>cs-teal-ground — teachr ground</p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <span class="box-container" style="background: #14a08d;color: #18181b;padding:8px;font-weight:700;">
          #14A08D
          <p>cs-teal-base — teachr accent</p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <span class="box-container" style="background: #d50e95;color: #fff;padding:8px;font-weight:700;">
          #D50E95
          <p>cs-pink-ground — ecommerce ground</p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <span class="box-container" style="background: #c10d82;color: #ebf5ff;padding:8px;font-weight:700;">
          #C10D82
          <p>cs-pink-deep — ecommerce deep accent</p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <span class="box-container" style="background: #d73735;color: #fff;padding:8px;font-weight:700;">
          #D73735
          <p>cs-red — brand accent (= $vb-primary)</p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <span class="box-container" style="background: #e34a47;color: #18181b;padding:8px;font-weight:700;">
          #E34A47
          <p>cs-red-lifted — red for dark grounds (visuAI)</p>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
{% endmacro %}
